+### Form floating classes
+
+The floating-label key ships the container, the floated geometry of the text control, the plaintext
+control, and the select inside it, the label with its transforms under focus, when filled, and when
+autofilled, the reduced-motion twin of the label transition, the textarea label backdrop, and the
+disabled and plaintext labels. The component partial loads after the range partial in the components
+layer. The validation rules the release records against the container ship from the validation
+partial, and the input-group rules it records there belong to the input-group family.
+
+The label sits over its control and fills the container. At rest its inset matches the control's
+own, so the label's text sits where the control's text would, and its transparent border matches the
+control's border width for the same reason. Keyboard focus, a value, or an autofill scales the label
+to `0.85` of its size from its top-left corner and lifts it, and the control's text moves down to
+the floated top inset beneath it. A select's label and a plaintext control's label are floated at
+rest. The label's text is the body color at `0.65` alpha, so it reads as a hint over the control
+rather than as the control's value. A control reports itself empty through `:placeholder-shown` only
+when it carries a placeholder, so each floating control carries one, and the partial hides the
+placeholder text so the label alone names the control at rest.
+
+A textarea's text scrolls under its floated label, so the label paints a backdrop behind its own
+text on the body surface whenever the textarea is focused or filled, and on the secondary surface
+when the textarea is `disabled`. The plaintext control draws its border on the block axis alone, and
+its label does the same. The label of a `disabled` control paints `--vn-gray-600`, which holds the
+release's own gray in both color modes.
+
+These are the key's recorded departures.
+
+- **The insets read the density scale.** The resting inset of the label and the control, the
+  select's start inset, the floated bottom inset, and the backdrop's inset read `--vn-space-8`,
+  `--vn-space-6`, `--vn-space-5`, and `--vn-space-3`, the tokens that resolve to the release's
+  lengths. No token resolves to the control's `3.5rem` height or to the `1.625rem` floated top
+  inset, so both stay the release's literals, and so do the line height, the backdrop's `em` height,
+  the stacking, and the transform. A `--vn-factor-density` retune therefore moves the insets and
+  leaves the height and the floated top inset in place: at a factor of 2 an empty control's resting
+  insets outgrow the declared height, and that control grows past the height a filled one keeps.
+- **The disabled label reads the gray token.** The release compiles `#6c757d`; the partial writes
+  `var(--vn-gray-600)`, which resolves to that color and holds it in both modes.
+- **The height is written as one sum.** The release writes
+  `calc(3.5rem + calc(var(--bs-border-width) * 2))`; Sass flattens the nested call to
+  `calc(3.5rem + var(--bs-border-width) * 2)`, which computes the same height.
+
+The transform and its origin are the release's own bytes in the source, so the comparison records no
+difference there. The build spells the trailing `translateX(0.15rem)` as the equivalent
+`translate(0.15rem)` in the published stylesheet, and the resolved matrix the proof reads is the
+release's. The border width, the body color, the body and secondary surfaces, and the backdrop
+radius read the `--bs-*` variables the release names, so each declaration matches the release's own
+text and moves with a consumer's retune of that variable.
+
+[The floating label classes](../tests/src/styles/components/form-floating.test.ts) reads the
+resolved treatment in the browser: the container's positioning, each control's height and insets at
+rest, under keyboard focus, and after typing, the label's position, fade, transform, and origin in
+each of those states, the backdrop's geometry and its `disabled` surface, the plaintext label's
+border, the disabled label's gray, and the transition at rest and under the staged reduced-motion
+preference, beside the density, radius, and color-mode readings and a retune of each `--bs-*`
+variable the family reads. Each limit that bounds what the proof can claim is recorded beside the
+reading it bounds. No script can put a control into the autofilled state, so the autofill rules have
+no resolved reading, and the proof reads the declarations the cascade authors for them, which is
+compiled-contract evidence rather than a rendered proof. The class-qualified disabled label rule
+paints what the bare disabled rule already paints, so it takes the same declaration reading.
+Chromium resets the line height of a select that keeps its native appearance to `normal`, so the
+select's floated line height is read as a declaration until the select family ships the rule that
+removes that appearance. The control's own border, radius, and paint belong to the `.form-control`
+and `.form-select` rules, which this tree does not ship yet, so the frames the capture journey
+writes show the floated geometry over the bare controls; the reading of the floated label against a
+styled control waits on those families.
